Make the limit of the GBNF repetition check configurable. The check
multiplies the size of a repeated group by its repetition count and fails
above 2000, which the grammar of a large tool set exceeds: one group with
many alternatives under a `*`. LLAMA_GRAMMAR_MAX_REPETITION, when set to a
positive number, replaces 2000; LocalAI sets it from the
grammar_max_repetition model option (default 100000). Upstream proposals to
raise or configure the limit: ggml-org/llama.cpp#20867 and the PRs linked
there. Drop this patch when the pin has an equivalent.

diff --git a/src/llama-grammar.cpp b/src/llama-grammar.cpp
--- a/src/llama-grammar.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-grammar.cpp
@@ -11,8 +11,22 @@
 #include <set>
 #include <numeric>
 #include <stdexcept>
+#include <cstdlib>
 
 #define MAX_REPETITION_THRESHOLD 2000
+
+// LocalAI: the limit of the repetition check below, from LLAMA_GRAMMAR_MAX_REPETITION
+// when it is set to a positive number. Grammars of large tool sets go over 2000.
+static uint64_t llama_grammar_max_repetition() {
+    const char * env = getenv("LLAMA_GRAMMAR_MAX_REPETITION");
+    if (env != nullptr) {
+        const unsigned long long v = strtoull(env, nullptr, 10);
+        if (v > 0) {
+            return v;
+        }
+    }
+    return MAX_REPETITION_THRESHOLD;
+}
 #define GRAMMAR_RECURSIVE_LIMIT 256
 //
 // helpers
@@ -560,7 +574,7 @@ const char * llama_grammar_parser::parse_sequence(
             total_rules = min_times;
         }
 
-        if (n_prev_rules * total_rules > MAX_REPETITION_THRESHOLD) {
+        if (n_prev_rules * total_rules > llama_grammar_max_repetition()) {
             throw std::runtime_error("number of rules that are going to be repeated multiplied by the new repetition exceeds sane defaults, please reduce the number of repetitions or rule complexity");
         }
 
